From 992cd09c5c8465e64b6a0e1cad536dc3870ea033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Capture tool evidence from unverified students, and file it
 on verification

A student is only VERIFIED once the Google Form warm-up is submitted - opening
it does nothing, typing answers does nothing. Until then studentId is empty,
and reportToolResult dropped every result they produced. That is not an edge
case: a late arrival, anyone who never presses submit, any Apps Script hiccup.
They worked the manipulative all period and the proficiency spine saw nothing.

- Unverified devices now buffer each result to localStorage (bounded at 300)
  instead of discarding it. Nothing UNATTRIBUTED is ever written to the server,
  so the privacy posture is unchanged - the work simply waits on the device.
- flushPendingToolResults posts the buffer the instant saveVerifiedStudentJoin
  completes, so submitting the warm-up at minute 40 still files the whole
  period. It also retries on each poll tick, so a verification that landed
  during a network blip is not stranded until tomorrow.
- A partial flush keeps what did not send rather than dropping the remainder.
- If a student never verifies, nothing lands. That is the honest outcome and it
  is what the teacher-visible unverified count is for.

Also fixed: the day tally was keyed by studentId, so a student who verified
mid-lesson started a fresh tally and silently discarded every attempt made
before submitting the warm-up. It is keyed by session now, which is what the
per-device tally actually represents.

reportToolResult no longer requires the browser Supabase client on the secure
path, where it posts through /api/student/tool-evidence and never touches
supabase - a deploy where getSupabase() returned null recorded ZERO evidence,
silently. Same defect shape as the live_flow publish guard in /control.

Also added /distributive-area, /area-explorer and /balance-beam to ClassSync's
CLASS_MODE_TARGETS; all three are valid LiveToolRoute values, so broadcasting
one sent students to a destination the listener refused to navigate to.

